# Amendment 1.0.7: admit and place finite package forests separately

U12 retains its original U09/U10 dependencies, paths, package converter/style/interaction tasks and every native, fractional, measurement, worker, persistence, accessibility and actual UI gate. This amendment adds U12a admission followed by U12b placement as finite geometry prerequisites. No numeric bridge, implementation lease, held registration or feature acceptance is granted.

## Assign every donor line and retain every original test

F18/#39 donor `syson-layout/src/containers.rs` has 368 lines, SHA-256 `9d86a510de50586ffaacabb14ecb54415493d6888d9457ec87783b3399d1bec8`. Its complete `tests/containers.rs` has 553 lines/15 tests, SHA-256 `e486c5c2e96b07d786f772ee322c83762db24ba3ef70bd6bc81c2fbaff393aea`.

U12a receives lines 1–69 and 85–210: 195 lines, assigned-byte SHA `ed06f55748e6b7802914dc0dd8f3be7ae0a4d8cbce88e266c14a5d53238c3d7d`. U12b receives 70–84 and 211–368: 173 lines, SHA `f817f6e95f8eca613327bf56094926fb4f0cf3a0107a4caf96e821f1d178a98f`. Preserve all original tests byte-for-byte on the final `containers::layout_packages` wrapper. Imported obsolete private U10 helpers require counted owned replacements or actual public interfaces, never restoring U10 Guard fields.

## U12a: canonical forest admission

Bind landed U10b #175, merge `974e7591ec4296db96644954edb4d4daf71f41d6`, crate tree `fa12c1312c969adac6f9d30cffe130dec36a28f7`, placement SHA `cd5de614196e30f55082c0ec68ffe9680936678dde19e3f5faa141fb2bbcfb01`. Preserve public package types/errors and defaults. Validate all geometry/options even when unused, IDs, parents, cycles/depths, sibling-only edges, canonical ordering, checked work and fallible buffers. Preserve node/edge/work/ID/workspace defaults and the logical 4096*N+1024*E accounting; review simultaneously live forest/group storage without treating it as heap/RSS.

Return an opaque forest token with immutable parent/order/index buffers and its own private ForestBudget/original callback/spent work. No public construction, reset, guard replacement or independent graph/guard recombination. Do not access, expose or construct U10 Guard. Exact/over limits, malformed forests, permutations, immutability and initial/interior/publication cancellation require actual public tests.

## U12b: sibling placement and atomic projection

After U12a is reviewed, landed and locally qualified, pin its exact source and consume once. Preserve bottom-up sibling layout, parent/header/border offsets, retained-position clamps and permitted retained overlap, default versus user-minimum sizing and relative/absolute projection. Each actual U10b call receives only remaining outer work and the same borrowed callback; debit each successful returned charged_work exactly once. Charge outer scans/projection and return no partial layout on any failure.

Add multiple nonempty sibling groups where each fits a reset quota but their total plus admission does not; require typed Work refusal. Exercise between-group and late cancellation, late-group failure after earlier success, empty publication and unchanged inputs. Execute all 15 original tests plus actual admission/continuation checks. Retain fractional Package measurement lineage without claiming Note/DOM/font/native equivalence.

## Dependencies, ownership and ordinary budgets

The finite chain is actual U10b→U12a→U12b. U12 keeps U09/U10 and adds U12b to implementation readiness plus both accepted children. Child source readiness does not require full parent feature acceptance. Exclusive module/test leases follow adoption; root owns containers/mod.rs, crate lib/manifests/lock/notices and serialized execution. No source/runtime work follows from this document alone.

Targets including wiring are U12a 340 production/700 authored and U12b 280/890. Hard caps remain 400 changed handwritten production/900 authored, additions plus deletions including imports/helpers/tests/wiring. The 553 unchanged original test lines count. Split another meaningful operation before writing oversized source; never minify or drop tests. Keep profilers separate. Use matched ordinary 32/64 and admitted 128/256/guarded 1024 ramps, two warmups/seven measured ranges and distinct allocation/live/RSS/work; p95 needs 30 samples and a declared estimator. Existing performance ranges remain unchanged.

## Full preservation and remaining acceptance

Contract 1.0.7 retains all 788 prior units and 55 historic records and adds U12a/U12b for 790 units/1,580 readiness nodes. Earlier sealed policy objects, amendments, history, holds and performance bytes remain intact. The new typed policy validates before compatibility exclusions. The full verifier reconstructs every 788 original normalized record, retaining unknown extra fields; older routing's 786-record proof restores only the new forest delegation/C99 dependencies/C08 derived joint inputs before its existing restoration. C08 already depends on U12, so its closure grows from 611 to 613 and must retain both new forest inputs and implementation edges. C04 and C09 do not depend on U12; retain their exact 608/610 closures without inventing new prerequisites.

Finite geometry does not complete U12. Native package converter/style/icons/compartments, measurement→layout→routing, fractional policy, resize/move/rotate, worker staleness/cancellation, persistence, focus/accessibility and actual pointer/keyboard undo/reload remain open. Require matched native/source/artifact evidence, 320/1440 px and 200/400% zoom, readable labels/edges and actual consuming main caller. Preserve #130 and its 12 held registrations; no old UI result transfers automatically.
